  "textHash": "1a00d056c4033da2113c8013d10548dd0c5944109a46377913d5f76184b0db66",
  "text": "Notary is an agent that won't touch money until it has proven how its tools behave. It reads the docs and turns every promise into a claim. Before each test call, it commits a prediction, hashed, so it can't change afterwards. Then it calls the API and compares. A Reflector proposes explanations. A stronger Adversary, running on a different model, tries to refute them. In our runs, it narrowed all five beliefs instead of rubber-stamping them. What survives becomes a certificate, valid only where it was tested. And the rule is simple. No certificate, no money moves. The Guard holds anything uncovered for a person to review.",
